Webhook body status was trusted (status from the Datatrans API was fetched only for redirect
returns), so a forged webhook could mark an unpaid order as paid; always take the status from the API.
When a webhook HMAC key is configured, a request without the Datatrans-Signature header skipped
verification; reject it. Without a configured key webhooks are still accepted (HMAC stays optional).

